{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/818150-an-alternate-approach-to-sidereal-charms","id":818150,"title":"An alternate approach to sidereal charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-27T19:32:51-08:00","id":818150,"title":"An alternate approach to sidereal charms","content":"I'm not proposing a re-write and I know 3e wont go this way, but it was an idea I had and sidereals already have shades of it.<br /> <br /> Sidereals draw their power from what could have been. Futures are not set, just possiblities, threads of fate that hadn't been woven into the &quot;present&quot;. Normally when certain fates become cut off the remnant threads float around until that no longer possible future has passed and they are recycled. Sidereals however can draw on these remnants and force that impossibility into reality. For example a door is locked, but there was once a potential thread of fate where it wasn't. The sidereal grabs that cut thread and rewrites its current future to unlock the door. Instead of storing a weapon in elsewhere they draw it from a timeline where they had it on them already.<br /> <br /> Think Bioshock Infinite","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7554-praise-the-sun","name":"Praise the Sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T19:37:29-08:00","id":818151,"title":"","content":"Completely random, but this is basically how magic in the Deathgate Cycle worked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T00:17:56-08:00","id":818254,"title":"","content":"Cool idea. Sounds like Getimian Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T00:35:08-08:00","id":818261,"title":"","content":"Maybe. Maybe not. We don't know much about them yet.<br /> <br /> But it definitely sounds like <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/threads/pdf-nocturnals-2e.51588/\" target=\"_blank\">Reminiscent Oasis' Nocturnal Exalted</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T01:06:02-08:00","id":818276,"title":"","content":"It's not a bad idea, may be how Getimians work, sort of (I get the impression they're more disrupting fate generally in strategic ways, than finding the lost threads though).<br /> <br /> It's not so much what I'd emphasize for Sidereals, as I like the idea of characters who fill themselves with the essence of Secrets, Battles, Journeys, Endings, Serenity, and then use this to enhance their skills more compelling than the whole &quot;They just change reality to make it work out how they want&quot; element, which is close to wishcasting for me. If you get what I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T03:02:03-08:00","id":818311,"title":"","content":"Romans me of the nocturnals the chosen of Nox. Wasnt it dragonmystic whom made those<br /> <br /> Edit: siderealed and wrong","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}